I keep forgetting this command....

	bundle config set --local path vendor/bundle
	bundle exec jekyll serve

If net/http screeches something ugly because gitHub's CRL (whatever that means):

	Configuration file: /home/tree/view/our/fork/github.com/rapidcow/site-wisc-sdc-fa25-team/site/_config.yml
	To use retry middleware with Faraday v2.0+, install `faraday-retry` gem
		    Source: /home/tree/view/our/fork/github.com/rapidcow/site-wisc-sdc-fa25-team/site
	       Destination: /home/tree/view/our/fork/github.com/rapidcow/site-wisc-sdc-fa25-team/site/_site
	 Incremental build: disabled. Enable with --incremental
	      Generating...
	      Remote Theme: Using theme pages-themes/minimal
	jekyll 3.10.0 | Error:  SSL_connect returned=1 errno=0 peeraddr=140.82.112.10:443 state=error: certificate verify failed (unable to get certificate CRL)
	/usr/lib/ruby/3.4.0/net/protocol.rb:46:in 'OpenSSL::SSL::SSLSocket#connect_nonblock': SSL_connect returned=1 errno=0 peeraddr=140.82.112.10:443 state=error: certificate verify failed (unable to get certificate CRL) (OpenSSL::SSL::SSLError)
		from /usr/lib/ruby/3.4.0/net/protocol.rb:46:in 'Net::Protocol#ssl_socket_connect'

just tell it to shut up:

	echo 'OpenSSL::SSL::VERIFY_PEER = OpenSSL::SSL::VERIFY_NONE' >> shutupssl.rb
	RUBYOPT='-ropenssl -r./shutupssl.rb' bundle exec jekyll serve

(Trick learned from <https://stackoverflow.com/a/1113614>)

(Of course this means that MITM can happen, but idc that's what
happens when you require Internet connection for a stupid SSG >:(((
shame on you GitHub go write a 2500-word reflection on why you did this
